    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="18649b44-b940-5298-9671-04583478cb79" activityNameId="bfd1418a-4734-5951-b167-f0a36b9cc9fc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, high voltage, production HR, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, high voltage, production HR, at grid
Electricity domestic net production shares are based on annual averages for 2023. Losses are distributed across voltage levels with total losses for the same time frame as well as older proxy data for disaggregation. The transmission network and direct emissions to air (ozone and N2O) are also included. Remark: This dataset describes the transmission of high voltage electricity. Ozone- and NO2-emission factors are based on published measurements made in various countries. Assumptions for transmission network, losses and emissions are based on older UCTE data. UUID: e81797cf-cb18-3fb5-8f5a-63f4bd8d9f01
Included are the shares of domestic electricity production by technology at the busbar. Not included are transformation, transport or distribution losses.
Location: Data apply to utilities and auto-producers.
Technology: No technology description is provided because the dataset just describes the power plant portfolio of the respective country using current average technology per energy carrier.
Time period: Time period of statistics used.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Statistical data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e81797cf-cb18-3fb5-8f5a-63f4bd8d9f01.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
